===============================================================================
3. THIRD-PARTY SOURCES
===============================================================================
The measurements in data/ are computed from metadata retrieved from external
services. Those services own their data and set their own terms; nothing above
grants rights over it.

  Semantic Scholar Academic Graph API - paper metadata, abstracts and SPECTER2
  embeddings. Data licensed CC BY-NC 4.0 for the corpus as distributed by AI2.
  https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api

  OpenAlex - keywords and topics, used for the bottom-up candidate branch.
  Released as CC0 (public domain).
  https://openalex.org/

  arXiv - the paper set counted here consists of arXiv preprints. Titles and
  abstracts belong to their authors; per-paper licences vary.
  https://arxiv.org/

  MIT AI Risk Repository (arXiv:2408.12622) - the 7-domain / 24-subdomain risk
  taxonomy that src/common.py reproduces verbatim in order to map the glossary
  onto it. Credit to Slattery et al.
  https://airisk.mit.edu/
